#!spectest
# mode: run
# adjudicator: ggdef
# since: spec-v0.1
# features: [move, liveness]
# doc: |
#   May-move static rejection (verdict = elaborate ∘ eval). `x` is moved into
#   `sink(!x)`, then read by `print(x)`. The flow-sensitive liveness gate rejects
#   it BEFORE eval with E_UseAfterMove — stdout stays EXACTLY empty (the program
#   never ran, which IS the verdict), exit 1. This fixture proves the reject
#   verdict-triple AND the E_-code conformance axis: flipping the expected
#   `reject:` code must make this lane MISMATCH (Core #6/#8).
# expect:
#   exit: 1
#   stdout: ""
#   reject: E_UseAfterMove
#!end

void sink(String !s):
    pass

void main():
    String x = "hi"
    sink(!x)
    print(x)
